# tools/s/scrubber_witness.rish -- the playback scrubber proves itself over moving video (Season G, open media).
#
# Season G (Open Media Primitives) - the rung beside image/text_subtitle.rye. Where a subtitle track pins timed TEXT over
# a moving reel, a scrubber pins timed GEOMETRY: the playback progress bar a video player draws along the bottom edge, its
# elapsed portion growing left to right as the clip plays. image/scrubber.rye renders the same mostly-still moving
# background, then composites a fixed-place bar onto each frame whose fill width is a pure function of playback progress.
#
# The crux this witness proves is that the elapsed fill is a monotone, data-driven function of the frame index: the count
# of elapsed pixels is non-decreasing frame to frame and strictly grows from empty (frame zero) to full (the last frame),
# a scrubbed frame differs from the background only within the scrubber rectangle, and the whole reel round-trips byte for
# byte through BOTH open codecs; the delta/keyframe mix is REPORTED, never claimed a compression win (REDS %82). No
# network, no key, no funds -- integer arithmetic maps progress to a pixel width, so no float ever enters.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/s/scrubber_witness.rish

say "scrubber: Language EN -- Season G's timed-geometry rung; a playback progress bar whose elapsed fill is a pure function of the frame index, composing image/shape.rye onto image/frames.rye and image/frames_delta.rye."
say "scrubber: Style Radiant -- the bar holds its place while its fill grows with playback; empty at the first frame, full at the last, and never a column running backward between them."
say "scrubber: Lens TAME -- u32 in-memory counts, u8 pixel bytes; the progress map is integer arithmetic in u64 narrowed once proven <= inner width, so no float enters; every buffer names a maximum (scrubber_max_frames, the codecs' encoded_bound, the QOI ceilings beneath); the bar is validated before a pixel is painted; each failure has a name; the delta/keyframe mix a reported measurement, never a false compression claim; no network, no key, no funds."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "image/bin/scrubber"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p image/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build image/scrubber.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "scrubber: build failed -- ${build.err}"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "scrubber: selftest exited non-zero -- ${selftest.out}"

let out = trim selftest.out
say "scrubber: ${out}"

assert selftest.out contains "GREEN image-scrubber" else "scrubber: selftest did not print the GREEN scrubber line"

assert selftest.out contains "elapsed fill grows" else "scrubber: the monotone-fill crux (empty first frame, full last) did not prove"

assert selftest.out contains "touching only the" else "scrubber: the overlay-touches-only-the-bar crux did not prove"

assert selftest.out contains "round-trip byte-identical through BOTH codecs" else "scrubber: the scrubbed reel did not round-trip through both codecs"

say "scrubber: GREEN -- a playback progress bar over moving video; the elapsed fill grows monotone from empty to full as a pure function of the frame index, touching only the bar, and the composited reel round-trips byte for byte through both open codecs."
